-- title:
--   Čerednik–Drinfeld fine-level family on all Noetherian bases
-- statement:
--   The data of the statement are organised as follows; the conclusion is stated in full at the end.
--
--   **Numerical and local data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`) and a non-zero natural number $N$ which is squarefree (`hN`) and divisible by neither $r$ (`hrN`) nor $\bar r$ (`hrbarN`). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`) such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), with residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ a characteristic-zero field which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (written `Onr`) which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $F$ (`Fr`), subject to the group `hOnr_complete`, `hOnr_max`, `hOnr_alg`, `hOnr_closed`, `hFr`: $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$, and $F(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$. A monoid homomorphism $v_{\det}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ with $v_{\det}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side and moduli.** A quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ which is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and whose completion at a finite place is a division algebra exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), with maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`) containing all rational integers (`hΛℤ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point assignment `pt` making it a coarse moduli scheme for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ (`h𝒳`). An auxiliary level $n\ge 3$ (`hn`) prime to $r$ (`hrn`), to $\bar r$ (`hrbarn`) and to $N$ (`hnN`); a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptF` a fine moduli family for fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`); a group $G$ acting on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ satisfying `IsLevelTwistAction` (`hρ`), so that $\rho(g)$ lies over the base and realises the twist by $\chi(g)$ of level structures, the labels being multiplicative, exhaustive and faithful modulo $n$. A morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under the $G$-action (`hρp`) and compatible with the point assignments (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke and Atkin–Lehner structure.** For every prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptT` a coarse moduli family for fake elliptic curves with extra $\ell$-level (`h𝒴`), together with degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) which on points forget the $\ell$-level (`hd₀`) and pass to the $\ell$-isogenous curve (`hd₁`); endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) inducing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** A quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ with $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, ramified exactly at the places above $\bar r$ (`hdef`); a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`), an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`); an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); the place $v$ above $r$ (`hv`). The subgroup $\Gamma^{t}$ consisting of the units integral at all places other than $v$ (`hΓt`); elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $s^{f}_\ell$ for each $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ whose four conditions (`hs`) state that the component of $s^f_\ell$ at a place not above $r$ is $s_\ell$, that its component above $r$ is $1$, that the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ times $(s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and that $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; the groups $\Gamma^t_\ell=\Gamma^t\cap s_\ell\Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^t$ (`hwbar`). A coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}(r)^2$ which is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product rule, is injective, has dense image modulo all powers of $r$, and is compatible with reduced traces (`hcoord`).
--
--   **Data on the special fibre.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ of level $N$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ over that ring of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ in two variables for $A_0$ identifying $A_0$ formally with $X_0$ through $\mathrm{coord}$ (`hA₀`); families $e,e'\colon\Gamma^t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`he`) with degrees $\deg$. The clauses on these: each pair $(e_\gamma,e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure (`hE1`); $e$ is multiplicative up to powers of $r$ (`hE1mul`); rational scalars in $\Gamma^t$ act through $A_0$'s $\Lambda$-action up to powers of $r$ (`hE1sc`), and conversely $e_\gamma$ scalar up to a power of $r$ forces $\gamma$ scalar (`hE1'`); for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma$ is matched by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser inducing $e_\gamma$ on formal coordinates with $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$ (`hE2`); every full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ admits labels $\mathrm{lab}\colon\Gamma^t\to\Lambda$ describing the action of $e_\gamma$ on $P_0$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$ (`hE3`); and every $r$-power isogeny self-map, level-preserving, of a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$ up to powers of $r$ (`hE4`). An order $R_2\le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂r`) and a family $\hat e$ on $R_2$ over the base (`hê`) which is additive, $\Lambda$-equivariant and level-preserving (`hE5a`), unital, multiplicative and matching the $\Lambda$-action on integers (`hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`), satisfies $\hat e_{\bar x}\circ \hat e_x=\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{nrd}\,x)$ (`hE5c`), is compatible with $e_\gamma$ for $x=r^{k}\gamma$ (`hE5d`), and admits a single $\mathrm{GL}_2$-normalisation simultaneously for $\Gamma^t$ and for $R_2$ (`hE5e`).
--
--   **Drinfeld uniformisation data.** A ring map $\iota\colon\mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special for $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`) together with $\eta$ assigning to rigidified objects points of $MD$, whose three clauses (`hη`) state that $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is compatible with base change, and is locally surjective on admissible objects over a Zariski cover; an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the sense of `hE₀` (some $m$ with $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ inside the image and $r^{m}$ times the image inside $M_2(\mathcal O)$). A family $e^{D}$ of maps from the functor of $G$-points $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\ \mathcal O\ MD$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with the formal upper half-plane functor $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$ of Deligne data, which is natural (`hnatD`), bijective on every Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra (`hbijD`), has the leg $\psi$ as first component (`hfstD`), translates the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points into the $v_{\det}$-twisted action on the product functor (`hGLD`), sends the $\pi$-translate relation to the Frobenius twist of the leg with unchanged Deligne datum (`hPiD`), $\pi$-translates existing always (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Transport and comparison data.** A ring map $\kappa\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ pushed along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`); a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on $A_0$: a curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ over the base realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny pair (`hBSw`) preserving level (`hBSwlev`), and a joint $\mathrm{GL}_2$-normalisation matching $\Gamma^t$ with $\iota_0$ and $a_w\circ b_w$ (in diagrammatic order $a_w$ followed by $b_w$) with $\iota_0(\bar w)$ (`hJOINTw`). A family $\Xi$ assigning to each Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, each leg $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ and each rigidified fake elliptic curve over $B$ a $G$-point of $MD$, with: the leg of $\Xi$ a Frobenius twist of $\psi$ over connected $B$ (`hΞleg`), compatibility with base change of rigidified curves (`hΞnat`), invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves matching the rigidifications up to powers of $r$ (`hΞiso`), and, over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, the explicit description $\Xi=\eta(t)$ for a rigidified object $t$ obtained by transport with $j\le 1$ and admissible for the twisted leg (`hΞdef`). An element $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and: translation of a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds to the action by $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ (`heqΓ`), the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ corresponds to the action by $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ (`heqW`); the four clauses `hK1`–`hK4` asserting, over connected Noetherian bases, existence of a rigidified pair whose image under $\Xi$ followed by $e^{D}$ is $g_0^{-1}$-twisted-equal to a prescribed pair $(\psi,P)$, uniqueness of such a pair up to an isomorphism compatible with the rigidifications, existence of its base change along any $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and a lifting clause along a surjection $B\to B_0$ whose kernel squares to zero; and `hC0e`, `hC0u` asserting existence, and uniqueness of the underlying point, of a level-$n$ structure on $E$ which is the height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along the rigidification.
--
--   **The given family on connected bases.** A family $\Theta_c$ which, for each Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ all of whose idempotents are $0$ or $1$, sends a triple $((\psi,P),g)$ with $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ and $g\in G$ to a point of $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}B$; $\Theta_c$ is natural in $B$ (`hΘcnat`), satisfies $\Theta_c(x,gh)$ followed by $\rho(h)$ equal to $\Theta_c(x,g)$ (`hΘcG`), has the value $\Theta_c((\psi,P),g)=\mathrm{ptF}\langle E,P_n\rangle$ followed by $\rho(g^{-1})$ whenever $(E,\varrho)$ is a rigidified pair with the prescribed leg and $g_0^{-1}$-twisted image $(\psi,P)$ and $P_n$ is a height-normalised transport of $P_0$ (`hΘcval`), and satisfies $\Theta_c((\psi,P),g)$ followed by $p$ equal to $\mathrm{pt}(E)$ for such a pair (`hΘcvalc`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a family $\Theta_f$ defined on *all* Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, with no connectedness assumption, sending a triple $((\psi,P),g)$ in $((O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\Omega_{K_0,\pi}(B))\times G$ to a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B\to M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, such that:
--
--   1.
--
--   $\Theta_f$ is natural: for Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, $B'$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi\colon B\to B'$, the value of $\Theta_f$ at $B'$ on the image of $x$ equals the image under $\varphi$ of $\Theta_f$ at $B$ on $x$;
--
--   2.
--
--   $\Theta_f$ is $G$-equivariant: for every $x$ in $(O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\Omega_{K_0,\pi}(B)$ and all $g,h\in G$, the point $\Theta_f(x,gh)$ followed by $\rho(h)$ equals $\Theta_f(x,g)$;
--
--   3.
--
--   the value clause holds on every Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent base: for all such $B$, every $\psi$, every Deligne datum $P$, every $g\in G$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ of level $N$ over $B$ with a rigidification $\varrho$ relative to $A_0$ over the leg $F^{-v_{\det}(g_0)}\psi$, and every full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$, if the leg of $\Xi(\langle E,\varrho\rangle)$ is that twisted leg, if $e^{D}(\Xi\langle E,\varrho\rangle)$ and $(\psi,P)$ are related by the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action, and if $P_n$ is a height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$, then the morphism underlying $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g)$ is $\mathrm{ptF}_B\langle E,P_n\rangle$ followed by $\rho(g^{-1})$;
--
--   4.
--
--   compatibility with the projection to the coarse moduli scheme on every Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent base: under the same hypotheses on $\psi$, $P$, $g$, $E$, $\varrho$ (the leg condition and the twisted-action condition), the morphism underlying $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g)$ followed by $p$ equals $\mathrm{pt}_B(E)$.
--
--   This is the globalisation step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the fine moduli scheme of fake elliptic curves with auxiliary level: a family of $M$-points constructed from Drinfeld's description of special formal modules is available only over connected $\pi$-nilpotent test algebras, and here it is extended to all Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent bases while retaining naturality, $G$-equivariance, the value on height-normalised transported level structures and the compatibility with the projection to the coarse moduli scheme. It feeds the construction of the full uniformising family in [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_fineFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_conn`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_fineFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_conn).
